  "description": "The all-new Kinesis Tripster AT gravel adventure frameset builds on the proven success of the legendary Tripster ATR and Kinesis’ championship-winning cyclocross heritage. Designed as a true all-terrain adventure bike, the new Tripster AT is engineered to excel across an incredibly broad range of riding styles and surfaces.\nBuilt around modern adventure bike standards, the Tripster AT delivers outstanding versatility. From daily commuting and long-distance gravel riding to bikepacking, touring, and bridleway exploration, this frameset is ready to adapt to whatever the ride demands.\nThe aluminium frame features front and rear thru-axles for confident handling and stiffness, with generous tyre clearance for 700c x 45mm or 650B x 52mm tyres. Flexible internal cable routing supports a wide range of drivetrain options, making the Tripster AT compatible with mechanical or electronic groupsets.\nPracticality is built in throughout, with multiple bottle cage mounts, rack and mudguard compatibility, and a durable British Standard threaded bottom bracket for long-term reliability and easy servicing. The frameset is completed with the premium Columbus Futura Cross+ carbon fork, delivering precise steering and all-day comfort, and is finished with Kinesis UK’s proven adventure geometry for stability and control on rough terrain.\nWherever the route leads, the Kinesis Tripster AT is a dependable, go-anywhere gravel frameset built for real-world adventure.\nWhat else has been updated for the Tripster AT?• New colours• Updated and improved geometry and sizing to match ATR• New, wider size range 48cm – 62cm• New and improved cable routing• New top tube pack mounting\n\nTripster AT Frame Parts Guide",
